--[[
The Dry Harbor: the harbor of the Salt, dry since the tide fell. The quay (a height above the seabed): the harbor office
(a fire and a teleporter: the waystation of the Salt), the lighthouse and Beacon, the guild hall of the Salt (its vault
inside), the crane and its mirror, the cargo yard (watched by a crimson lens), the sealed gate of the Tide Road
(Nerissa's letter scratched next to it). The seabed below (ladders down the quay wall): stranded ships (one can be
entered: the captain's cabin), the last puddle of the tide (eels), the tunnel from the Diggings.

The vault of the Salt opens to the light of the lighthouse (the tablet of the guild hall). Nothing in the city burns:
the great lantern at the top of the tower is lit with the ember of the Watch (the frontier). Its lamp then throws a beam
east along the quay: turn the mirror of the crane down, push one mirror crate under it and another one into the corner
of the row, clear the crates in the way: the beam goes up to the crystal by the door of the guild hall.
The grapnel of the vault reaches the mooring ring of the ledge, across the void of the cliff: the stairs up to the
Heights. A second ring, on the quay, brings the player back down from the ledge.
]]
